     1	//! plan-20260714 PD-00 follow-up guard: the THREE release version surfaces
     2	//! must stay in lockstep.
     3	//!
     4	//! PD-00 closed a drift where `Cargo.toml` and `web/package.json` were
     5	//! bumped but `install.sh`'s `DEFAULT_VERSION` fallback was left behind —
     6	//! a stale fallback silently installs an OLD binary whenever the release
     7	//! API is unreachable and `LIBRA_ALLOW_FALLBACK=1` is set. The card's
     8	//! explicit follow-up condition ("if it drifts again, add a guard that
     9	//! reads all files and asserts they agree") is what this target
    10	//! implements. PD-10 later added the Windows installer `$DefaultVersion`.
    11	//! plan-20260920 RC-36 removed the Publish `worker/` host, and the
    12	//! post-plan follow-up removed the whole `web/` tree, so the surfaces are
    13	//! now: `Cargo.toml`, `install.sh`, `install.ps1`.
