docs/commands/config.md:401:These flags provide backward compatibility with `git config` invocation patterns. They are hidden from `--help`. Most translate to the equivalent subcommand; `--remove-section` / `--rename-section` are flag-only section operations with no subcommand form.
docs/commands/config.md:411:| `--import` | `import` |
docs/commands/config.md:415:| `--remove-section <name>` | Delete the keys in section `<name>` in one transaction, using Git's section/subsection identity (so `--remove-section branch` removes `branch.<key>` but not the `branch.feature.*` subsection). Missing section → exit 128. |
docs/commands/config.md:416:| `--rename-section <old> <new>` | Move section `<old>`'s keys to `<new>`, preserving each value and its encryption flag. Missing source → exit 128; identical names → exit 2; an already-existing destination section is refused → exit 128. |
